2. TECHNICAL ARCHITECTURE & STACK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Frontend Stack:
- Framework: React 18 with TypeScript (Strict mode enabled)
- Bundler & Tooling: Vite 8 (Rolldown runtime)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v3 with CSS Variable RGB channel mapping
- Icons: Lucide React
- Testing Framework: Vitest with jsdom (18 unit/integration tests passing)
- Hash Routing: Hash-based routing (`/#/room/:roomId`) compatible with GitHub Pages

WebRTC & Media Pipeline:
- Native WebRTC APIs: `RTCPeerConnection`, `MediaDevices`, `getDisplayMedia`, `getUserMedia`.
- MediaStream Management: Handled via `src/webrtc/mediaManager.ts`. Handles dynamic track
  replacement (`replaceTrack`), automatic webcam restoration when screen share ends,
  and graceful device permission denial handling.
- Multi-Peer Mesh Topology: Managed via `src/webrtc/peerManager.ts` with ICE candidate queueing
  prior to remote description establishment.
- NAT Traversal & ICE: Configured in `src/webrtc/iceConfig.ts` with free Google STUN servers
  (`stun:stun.l.google.com:19302`, `stun:stun1.l.google.com:19302`) and user-configurable TURN.

Zero-Backend Global Cloud Signaling Architecture:
IMPORTANT: GitHub Pages is a static file host; it cannot execute Node.js, run WebSockets,
or run persistent server processes.
To enable multi-device communication over the internet without requiring users to host their
own server, ShareIt implements a 3-tier signaling strategy in `src/signaling/signalingClient.ts`:
  Tier 1 (Global Cloud Relay - Default):
    `src/signaling/mqttSignaling.ts`: Connects to public secure WebSocket MQTT brokers
    (`wss://broker.emqx.io:8084/mqtt`) scoping rooms to `shareit/v2/rooms/${roomId}`.
    Enables instant peer discovery across different computers, mobile devices, and Wi-Fi networks.
  Tier 2 (Custom Self-Hosted WebSocket):
    Connects to any RFC-compliant WebSocket server configured in Settings.
  Tier 3 (Local Same-Machine Fallback):
    `src/signaling/broadcastSignaling.ts`: Uses browser `BroadcastChannel` for offline
    testing between tabs on the same machine.

