3. THEME SYSTEM SPECIFICATION & IMPLEMENTATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The theme system allows seamless switching between 'dark', 'bw', and 'light'.

How it works under the hood:
1. `src/contexts/ThemeContext.tsx`:
   - Stores current theme in `localStorage.getItem('shareit_theme')`.
   - Modifies document root classes:
     * Dark: `html.dark`
     * B&W: `html.dark.theme-bw`
     * Light: `html.light`
2. `src/index.css`:
   - Defines CSS custom properties in space-separated RGB triplet format:
     * Dark: `--color-surface-950: 9 13 22;`, `--color-surface-900: 15 23 42;`, etc.
     * Light: `--color-surface-950: 248 250 252;`, `--color-surface-900: 255 255 255;`, etc.
     * B&W: `--color-surface-950: 0 0 0;`, `--color-surface-900: 10 10 10;`, `--color-brand-500: 255 255 255;`
3. `tailwind.config.js`:
   - Colors are defined with alpha placeholders:
     `surface: { 950: 'rgb(var(--color-surface-950) / <alpha-value>)', ... }`
   - This ensures all Tailwind opacity modifier classes (e.g. `bg-surface-950/80`,
     `border-surface-700/80`, `bg-surface-900/90`) work dynamically across all themes!
4. Black & White Contrast Rules:
   - When in `theme-bw`, `.bg-brand-500` buttons turn solid white (#ffffff).
   - Rules in `src/index.css` force button text and SVG icons to pure black (#000000)
     to maintain 100% contrast.
   - All headings (`h1` through `h4`) render in stark white with gradient overlays stripped.

