5. USER-DEFINED DESIGN RULES & INVARIANTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Rule 1: Landing Page UI Purity
  The landing page (`src/components/landing/LandingPage.tsx`) MUST strictly match the
  user's screenshot design:
  - Header: Logo icon + "ShareIt" brand, navigation links (Features, How It Works, Devices, FAQ),
    ThemeToggle, and "Start Sharing" button.
  - Hero: "Connect with anyone, anywhere." headline, clean subtitle text.
  - Centered Action Card:
    * Left side ("NEW MEETING"): Read-only generated room ID with copy button, and "Start Sharing" button.
    * Right side ("JOIN WITH CODE"): Text input with placeholder "e.g. share-xyz-123" and "Join Meeting" button.
    * Card Footer: 3 feature badges: "No install needed", "End-to-end encrypted", "100% Free".
  - DO NOT add marketing feature blocks, accordion FAQs, testimonials, or device cards to the landing page.

Rule 2: Global Theme Consistency
  Every view (Landing Page, Green Room, Meeting Stage, Video Grid, Video Tiles, Control Bar,
  Header, Chat, Participants, File Sharing, Settings, and Dialogs) MUST follow the active theme.
  Never hardcode `#090d16` or `text-white` on surfaces that change in light mode. Use semantic
  `bg-surface-*` and `text-surface-*` classes so that switching between Dark, B&W, and Light
  instantly updates the entire interface.

Rule 3: Cross-Device Signaling Reliability
  Do not default signaling to `localhost:8080`. The default signaling is the global cloud relay
  `MqttSignalingProvider` connecting over `wss://broker.emqx.io:8084/mqtt`, allowing participants
  on any device, phone, or remote network to connect seamlessly on GitHub Pages.

Rule 4: File Sharing Security
  Incoming files sent over WebRTC data channels must display an explicit "Accept / Reject" prompt.
  Never automatically download files onto the user's disk without consent.

